  "notes": "Source: official College of Staten Island undergraduate catalog (Coursedog), degree map 'CSC-BS | 2024-PRESENT' (Total Degree Map Credits 124-129; Degree Map Effective Catalog Year 2026-, i.e. 2026-2027). Transcribed 2026-09-30 from the catalog's term-by-term degree map (pp. 6-16 of catalog PDF generated 2025-09-16), cross-checked against the CSI CS department undergraduate page (www.cs.csi.cuny.edu/undergraduate.html) and the catalog program page. Raw catalog PDF: https://coursedog-pdfs-public-prod.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/csi01/catalog-pdf/ruWaU1g0EN9UVfQAV7q3/sMJm9FBaDQdn6EfcLHX0Od8Fg/CSC-CSI-2025-09-16-13-47-29.pdf. TOTAL: file uses 129 credits = the standard calculus-ready path (MTH 123 4cr, MTH 230+MTH 229 7cr, both 0-1cr ELEC 1000 slots taken at 1cr). Minimum 124 credits with MTH 130 (3cr), MTH 231+MTH 229 (4cr), and the two ELEC 1000 slots at 0cr. Minimum grade of C required in: CSC 126, CSC 211, CSC 228, CSC 315, CSC 430 (C in CSC 315 and CSC 330), CSC 346, MTH 232, MTH 233, and CSC electives I-III. A grade of C or above in CSC 126 is required for admission to the CS baccalaureate; CSC 126 not open to Engineering majors. Corequisites taken in the same term: CSC 346 + CSC 347, CSC 332 + CSC 305 (modeled as prereq links; CSC 346 is listed first in the map). CSC 490 requires senior standing in the CS major, ENG 151, and CSC 330 with C or higher. Alternate prerequisites for non-traditional routes (documented, not in term placement): CSC 326 accepts ENS 336; CSC 332 accepts ENS 362 in place of CSC 220; CSC 315 accepts ISI 300; CSC 446 accepts ENS/ENGR 220 in place of CSC 346; MTH 30 or appropriate CUNY math assessment may satisfy the MTH 1XX slot. ENG 111 requires a CUNY Proficiency Index score of 65+. The catalog's recommended career milestone (log in to Handshake account with Career Services, Fall Year 1) is included as a 0-credit required_zero milestone. The older 2023-2024 sample degree map on csi.cuny.edu (CSC 220 at 4cr then, now 3cr) was superseded and not used.",
